{"id":"resp_bc78248b20d986eb","created_at":1795550742,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9beb9ff41954b2d0","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to repair previous_candidate SHACL. The issue: ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR \"Unbounded/custom target route not supported by this admission boundary\". Means target must be within declared owner_class scope. Currently shapes use sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength . These are properties, not ensuring target within ship class. Admission expects target within ship population (owner_class ship). Should use sh:targetClass vocab:ship? Actually we already targetClass for ShipShape, but QuantityShape uses targetObjectsOf which is unbounded - not allowed. Should change to use sh:targetClass (maybe or sh:targetNode?) but need to apply to objects that are QuantityValue nodes owned by ship. The population boundary is ship class. The requirement: ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength are quantity values attached to ship. We can target them via sh:targetObjectsOf but admission doesn't allow custom target routes; must be limited to declared owner_class. So we need to anchor shapes via property paths from ship class. Use sh:property with sh:path vocab:ruleLength etc within ShipShape, which already does. QuantityShape may be used as node constraint for those property values, but we don't need separate target for QuantityShape; instead we embed within ShipShape property constraints for numericValue and unit. So remove sh:targetObjectsOf and define a node shape for quantity without targeting; then in ShipShape property, use sh:node ex:QuantityValueShape (or inline) with constraints on numericValue and unit. Already ShipShape uses sh:node ex:QuantityShape, but ex:QuantityShape is a NodeShape with its own target objects - causing error. Instead define ex:QuantityShape as a shape without target, just property constraints, and apply via sh:node. That should satisfy admission.\n\nAlso ensure canonical identifiers: use proper IRIs? Keep as is.\n\nThus modify ex:QuantityShape: remove sh:targetObjectsOf lines, keep just the constraints.\n\nAlso maybe we need to include sh:node on ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength? Already done.\n\nMake sure sh:equals is allowed? It may be okay.\n\nAlso maybe need to indicate sh:closed? Not required.\n\nThus produce revised SHACL.\n\nReturn whole block.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9bcd677145e3c48d","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/shapes#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that validates any QUDT QuantityValue used for rule lengths\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:QuantityShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    # The quantity must have a numeric value (decimal)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] ;\n    # The quantity must be expressed in metres\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Ship shape – enforces presence of the required length quantities\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    # L (the rule length used by the classification society) must be present\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:QuantityShape ;\n    ] ;\n    # The generic ruleLength property must also be present and must be the same\n    # quantity as the classificationSocietyRuleLength (L = ruleLength)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:ruleLength ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:QuantityShape ;\n        sh:equals vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":51075,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":64,"cache_write_tokens":51008,"input_tokens_per_turn":[51075],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[64]},"output_tokens":937,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":461,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[937],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":52012},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}